    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that \"steering wheel\" thing feels like a lie. like, if i have the same chemical imbalances they had, and the same brain structure, then the outcome is already decided. how can i be in control if the biology is already running the show? it just feels like i'm watching a movie i've already seen the ending to. it's exhausting to keep pretending i can change the script.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes sense that you feel trapped when the biology feels like a script written in advance, but the very fact that you're questioning the script means you're still writing new lines. Your brain's chemistry is a tool, not a verdict, and even if the foundation is cracked, you can still choose how to build on it. You don't have to believe you can fix everything today, just that the story isn't over until you stop turning the page.",
      "source": "target",
