      "content": "Accepting the inevitable is a terrible way to live, but the point is not to fight the gravity of your genes, it is to learn how to fall without breaking. Your biology is just a vehicle, not your destiny, and the only thing that truly decides your outcome is whether you choose to get out of it. You are not a passenger; you are the one who holds the keys to your own life, even if the road is long and difficult.",
